{
 "id": "Microwave",
 "slug": "microwave",
 "topic": "The microwave oven tells its own story (first-person narration; drawn as a green radar/vector CRT screen)",
 "title": [
  "I WAS",
  "AN ACCIDENT"
 ],
 "accent": "ACCIDENT",
 "voice": {
  "id": "pFZP5JQG7iQjIQuC4Bku",
  "model": "eleven_v4",
  "language": "en",
  "settings": {
   "stability": 0.5,
   "similarity_boost": 0.8,
   "style": 0.3,
   "use_speaker_boost": true
  }
 },
 "tail": 2.0,
 "lead": 2,
 "gap": 0.2,
 "tempo": 1.0,
 "script": [
  {
   "beat": "s",
   "text": "I was not invented. I was an accident. And it started with a melted candy bar."
  },
  {
   "beat": "s",
   "text": "Let me rewind."
  },
  {
   "beat": "s",
   "text": "Nineteen forty-five. My mother was a radar tube. A magnetron. Her job was hunting enemy planes."
  },
  {
   "beat": "s",
   "text": "One day, an engineer named Percy Spencer walked past her. A man who never finished grade school."
  },
  {
   "beat": "s",
   "text": "And the candy bar in his pocket turned to soup."
  },
  {
   "beat": "s",
   "text": "Most men would have changed their trousers. Percy fetched popcorn."
  },
  {
   "beat": "s",
   "text": "It popped. All over the lab."
  },
  {
   "beat": "s",
   "text": "Next, he tried an egg. It exploded. In a colleague's face."
  },
  {
   "beat": "s",
   "text": "And that, my friends, was my first meal."
  },
  {
   "beat": "s",
   "text": "Two years later, I went on sale. I was six feet tall. I weighed seven hundred and fifty pounds. And I cost about five thousand dollars."
  },
  {
   "beat": "s",
   "text": "Nobody wanted me."
  },
  {
   "beat": "s",
   "text": "So I went on a diet. Twenty years of it. Until, in nineteen sixty-seven, I finally fit on a kitchen counter."
  },
  {
   "beat": "s",
   "text": "Today, I live in nine out of ten American homes. That's real."
  },
  {
   "beat": "s",
   "text": "And what do you do with a machine born from war radar? You reheat yesterday's pizza."
  },
  {
   "beat": "s",
   "text": "You're welcome. Ding."
  }
 ],
 "science": [
  {
   "claim": "Percy Spencer (Raytheon), 1945: a candy bar melted in his pocket near an active magnetron; he then popped popcorn and exploded an egg",
